module SignatureTrailerCommentNotFloating exposing (withComment)

-- A comment BETWEEN a signature and its definition is never free-floating, so
-- it never takes the two-blank treatment -- however the author spaced it.
--
-- `floating` reads `infoDetachedBelow`, which is computed from the INPUT rows.
-- The gap it finds below this comment is the very gap `sigThenDef` closes two
-- iterations later when it pulls the definition up under the signature. So the
-- first format called the comment free-floating and gave it two blanks, moved
-- the definition up, and the reparse -- now seeing no gap below the comment --
-- called it not floating and gave it one. `p.sigPending` is the same span
-- `classifyChildren` and `sigThenDef` already read, so all three now agree.
--
-- The `-- trailing` on the signature row is what opens the gap above: without
-- it the comment abuts the signature and `gap` is False.


withComment : Int -- trailing

-- a note about the definition

withComment =
    1
